From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:28:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] compositor: use variable refresh only for windows that
 ask for it

Mutter switched a display with variable refresh turned on to variable
mode for any window that covered it. Video players and browsers then
drove the refresh rate with their irregular frame timing, and panels whose
brightness depends on the refresh rate, VA panels in particular, flicker.

Support wp_content_type_v1 and expose the content type a client declares
on MetaWindow, and add a variable-refresh window property that the shell
sets for windows it wants a display to follow. A display only leaves its
fixed rate while a window with that property covers it; everything else
keeps the display at the rate of its mode.

With com.lantharos.kestrel.diagnostics log-variable-refresh enabled, the
compositor logs whenever the window covering a display changes, whether
the refresh rate follows it and why not.
